fact WorkItem(id: "WI-650", description: some(value: "Map: drop the O(n^2) relational eq/binds/strip_is apparatus and back Eq[T=Map] at the operation level (KEEP provides Eq[T=Map] + a BODYLESS operation eq(a:Map,b:Map)->Bool; the provision is backed because the spec op Eq.eq is a builtin — op_backed path 3 — so the stdlib still loads). Consequence to guard: WI-616 SemEq dispatch (sem_eq_core -> sem_eq_dispatch, resolve.rs ~3592) sub-resolves the declared Map.eq override, finds NO rules, exhausts, and returns sem_verdict(false) = SILENTLY 'not equal' (order-sensitive structural-ish wrong answer). BuiltinResult has no error channel (Success/Delay/Failure only), so make it a LOUD TYPE-TIME diagnostic instead: an =/eq/neq (Eq.eq/Eq.neq) application whose operand sort declares its OWN eq override that has NO backing (no non-fact rules, no runnable body) is a compile error 'Eq[<sort>] declared but unimplemented (pending WI-625 host bridge)'. Per use-site: the stdlib never compares maps so it stays clean; only user code comparing maps errors. HOOK: mirror check_one_spec_op_requirement (typing.rs ~24636) which already reads each operand's inferred sort head via inferred_type()->sort_functor_of_view; but it returns early on is_builtin and Eq.eq IS a builtin, so add an eq-specific check BEFORE that skip (or a sibling pass) in BOTH the rule-body-goal pass and the op-body (WI-325) pass. Reuse an op_backed-style predicate for the carrier's OWN override (not the spec-op builtin path, which would mask it). TEST FALLOUT (wi616_semantic_eq_test.rs): DELETE map_eq_ignores_put_order / map_eq_honors_put_shadowing / map_eq_distinguishes_values_and_domains / map_binds_unifies_non_ground_stored_value (test the removed rules; general WI-624/633 invariants stay covered by the unbox0/unbox1 Box tests); re-vehicle dispatch_on_non_ground_operand_suspends_and_never_binds onto Set (keeps its eq); ADD a test asserting eq(map,map) in a rule/op body is a LOUD type error; update comments mentioning Map.binds. Follow-up to WI-627. Acceptance: Map has no relational eq/binds/strip_is; stdlib loads; a rule/op body comparing two Maps fails to load with the new diagnostic; Set eq unaffected; enums/ADTs keep structural eq; full suite green."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: nil), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-07-07T08:01:21Z"))
